### Expected behaviour

The UPF should validate the Dropped-DL-Traffic-Threshold IE by verifying the IE length against its encoded subfields.
If a malformed encoding is detected, the UPF should treat it as invalid input and handle the error gracefully.

### Observed Behaviour

When UPF receives a PFCP Session Establishment Request containing a CreateURR with a malformed Dropped-DL-Traffic-Threshold IE whose length field does not match the expected constant, the UPF crashes.

